  "description": "Try-Catch wrapping an HTTP GET against the http-echo service's armed timeout endpoint. The first request times out (HTTP plugin raises TimeoutError, pause-on-errors fires); the second request (after Repeat Step) hits the disarmed endpoint and returns instantly. Catch path logs 'caught', then path logs 'passed'. Final-attempt-wins semantics: after a successful Repeat, Continue routes through 'then' (not 'catch').",
